Task: Locate the anchor function for the req_sig field in the console.log object whose action is request.sign after filling API Endpoint with /api/v2/users, selecting HTTP Method POST, selecting Auth Scheme bearer, and clicking Generate Signature. The anchor is the first target-specific value-construction function on the dynamic behavior chain: it appears after routing, request action-table resolution, scope-field selection, and input preparation, and its own function body constructs the target request-signature hash value instead of merely collecting request parameters, forwarding control, wrapping a return value, or emitting to the sink. Return exactly one complete JavaScript function and its location in the captured corpus. Do not return a generic utility, event handler, action-table dispatcher, scope resolver, full call chain, or final console sink.

Example value pattern: ^sig_[a-z0-9]{12}$
Observable: {"type": "console", "method": "log", "action": "request.sign", "field": "req_sig", "format": "^sig_[a-z0-9]{12}$"}

Shortlisted functions:
### 26001f46af692637 (n0)
```js
function n0(envelope) {
  const payload = Object.freeze(buildPayload(envelope));
  paint(payload);
  console[methodName()](payload);
  return payload;
}
```
### 9b37b2db5e37f199 (tupleDigest)
```js
function tupleDigest(tuple) {
  let lane = 0x811c9dc5;
  for (const item of tuple) {
    const text = item.k + ":" + item.v + ":" + item.plain.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += 1) {
      lane = Math.imul((lane ^ text.charCodeAt(i)) >>> 0, 0x01000193) >>> 0;
    }
  }
  return lane.toString(36);
}
```

